course: dictionary
lesson: 1288
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Button is one of them. The sentence around it gives you the clues, so read those first and then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: «Press the button to start the lift.» The clue is press: you push something to make a machine work. «Button up your coat before you go out» is different. The clue is coat, so button means to close the coat with buttons.
explain: «An emergency stop button cuts the power at once and stays pressed in until someone has checked the problem.» The words emergency and power tell you a machine is being switched off quickly. Here button means a switch you press, not a small round thing on a shirt.
explain: Always try your meaning in the sentence. If it sounds silly, you have picked the wrong meaning. You do not press a shirt; you button it.
fact: A button can be a small round thing that holds clothes closed by going through a hole.
fact: A button can also be something you press to make a machine or screen work.
fact: A badge with a pin is also called a button.
fact: To button means to close something with buttons, as in «button up your coat».
fact: An event is something that starts code, like pressing button A. It is the same idea as "when green flag clicked" in Scratch.
exercise: «Press the button to start the lift.» What does button mean here? | *Something you press to make a machine work | To close with buttons | A small round thing that closes a coat | A badge with a pin
exercise: «Button up your coat before you go out.» What does button mean in this sentence? | *To close with buttons | A small round thing on a shirt | Something you press to make a screen work | A badge with a pin
exercise: Ayaan sorts his buttons by hole, size and colour. What are the buttons he is sorting? | Something you press to make a machine work | *Small round things that hold clothes closed | A badge with a pin | To close clothes
test: «An emergency stop button cuts the power at once.» What is the button in this sentence? | *A switch you press to stop a machine | A pin badge | A small round thing on a coat | To close something with buttons
test: Which sentence uses button as a verb, meaning to close with buttons? | The belly button is in the middle | Buttons sorted by colour | *Button your coat up before school | Press the button to start
exam: An event is something that starts code, like pressing button A. What does an event do in a program? | It closes a coat | It makes a badge with a pin | *It starts code to run | A stops the power at once
